<Base title="7. Build the hull — AquaSense">
  <p class="kicker">Step 7 of 9</p>
  <h1>Build the hull</h1>
  <p class="lede">24″ square of 4″ Schedule 40 PVC (SECOORA Levin BOB float), Pelican 1120 on the square, 10 W panel <em>on the lid</em>, cage with five sensors, mooring eye. Yellow or white only.</p>
  <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/exploded.svg`} alt="Exploded layers: solar on lid, Pelican 1120, 24 inch PVC square with three inner tubes, five-sensor cage, mooring" style="margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--line)" />
  <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/buoy-isometric.png`} alt="Labeled isometric: PVC square, Pelican, solar on lid, pH EC DO DS18B20 MS5803" style="margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--line)" />
  <p class="caption">The labeled isometric is the parts count. The dusk photo is the same hull in lighting — if a probe count disagrees, the exploded SVG wins.</p>

  <h2>What we copy from Levin — and what we don’t</h2>
  <p>
    Float geometry is from the
    <a href="https://secoora.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/default/files/webfm/about/classroom/documents/BOBBuildManual030410.pdf">SECOORA BOB build manual (Levin)</a>:
    a <strong>24″ square</strong> of 4″ Sch40. We do <strong>not</strong> copy the Pasco pegboard mast, GLX logger, or four-sensor Pasco cage. Deck on this kit is the Pelican 1120.
  </p>

  <h2>Cuts (adult + saw, eye protection)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>One 10 ft stick of 4″ Sch40 → <strong>eight 15″ pieces</strong> (Levin). Leftover is scrap.</li>
    <li>Four 15″ pieces + four 90° elbows = the outer ring. Dry-fit so it lies flat (stand on opposite corners) before cement.</li>
    <li>Levin: do not use instant-grab cement. Slow-set so you can still flatten the square.</li>
    <li>Three remaining 15″ pieces get a cap on <em>each</em> end (six caps) — inner floats, strapped inside the square.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Deck and solar</h2>
  <p>Strap the Pelican 1120 to the inner tubes so the lid opens above water. <strong>Solar panel on the closed lid</strong> — never a second box sitting on the cells. Glands on the bottom face only. Optional tray: <code>hardware/scad/tray.scad</code>.</p>

  <h2>Cage — five items, not six</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Three industrial probes: pH, EC, DO</li>
    <li>One thin DS18B20</li>
    <li>One small potted MS5803 breakout (not a long sixth probe)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Keep the cage off the bottom. Mooring eye on one corner of the square. Reflective tape. Paint yellow or white if you paint at all.</p>

  <div class="checkpoint">
    <strong>Checkpoint.</strong> You can see a hollow PVC <em>ring</em>, not a foam block. Solar is on the Pelican lid. Five sensors in the cage. Hull is yellow/white — not red/green.
  </div>
